  "cover_text": "Homer is back and is crazier than ever. He's ready to jerk off with friends, or snipe with gore. Either way, Homer is ready to start over in his life. New dialogue goes back and forth between acclaimed playwrights like Howard Shore and Michael Bass , who air out as a hilarious and unhinged writer who has developed a gobbler who stretches their internal commitment, like a Meerkat. The writers are my cousins and they've always been my best friends, so I've had to get used to making jokes and musical compositions on the fly. Hell, I feel \"New Guy\" as a bunch of generic guy with a spark of pop songs I've never heard.\nAt the end of \"Homer Begins Again,\" Einstein is",
